name wordnet-lexnames
# lexnames.5: "Each line in lexnames contains 3 tab separated fields ... The first field is the two digit decimal
# integer file number. ... The second field is the name of the lexicographer file that is represented by that number,
# and the third field is an integer that indicates the syntactic category of the synsets contained in the file."
# lexnames.5 gives these fields no names: each line is recorded as the tuple of its three fields, in its own order.
match lexnames
grammar table

claims
row tuple
